{{also|Boxen}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɒksən|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|boxen}}, replacing earlier {{m|enm|bixen}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|byxen||made of boxwood}}, equivalent to {{suffix|box|en|lang=en}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# Made of [[boxwood]].
# Resembling [[box]] (the wood).

===Etymology 2===
A nonstandard plural of {{m|en|box}} formed by analogy with {{m|en|oxen}}. The standard plural of ''box'' is {{m|en|boxes}}; ''-en'' is no longer a plural in standard use. See ''[[-en#Etymology 2|-en]]'' for details.

====Noun====
{{head|en|noun plural form}}

# (humorous) {{plural of|box||computer|lang=en}}

